silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_concrete_anchor a owl:NamedIndividual ;
    rdfs:label "InitialAlgebraConcreteAnchorExample" .
silm:instances_papers_00_whitepaper_chapters_01_signature_calculus_sections_04_initial_algebra_concrete_anchor silm:hasExample "In 'InitialAlgebraConcreteAnchor', the bare-symbol→anchor table grounds the abstract symbols in the Tartu-Animal-Clinic / Mittens-2026-05-18 domain story. For example, PublishTreeType: the type of all finite publish-operation trees; the initial Sigma-algebra carrier for the encyclopedia free monad; every encyclopedia entry (including VetRecord_77_tree for paper-00 and FelisCatusTSN183798_tree for the taxonomy leg) is an element of PublishTreeType; also, CataMorphism_VetRecord_Colimit: the catamorphism fold from PublishTreeType to MittensColimitApex; determined by the colimit structure map alpha: Sigma(MittensColimitApex) -> MittensColimitApex; maps VetRecord_77_tree to the record leg arrow VetRecord_77 -> MittensColimitApex; also, VetRecord_77_tree: the element of PublishTreeType (mu Sigma) representing the publish pipeline for VetRecord_77: the tree with root node render_node, child validate_node, grandchild type_node, and leaf ingest_node applied to TartuClinicIntakeForm; a concrete four-depth tree in the initial algebra." .
